    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:52.521%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:98.900%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="display:none"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top">
              <div>
                <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The allowance for funds used during construction (AFUDC) computation is not based on Viking Gas Transmission Company's (VGT) financial statement balances. The actual AFUDC calculation is based on the cost of debt, capital structure, forecasted short-term borrowings and average forecasted CWIP balances of DT Midstream, Inc. The cost rate of common equity is the most recent rate granted for common equity in a VGT proceeding.</span>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In July 2023, Viking filed with the FERC in Docket No. RP23-917-000 a proposed increase in rates pursuant to Section 4 of the Natural Gas Act of 1938. In February 2024, the participants reached a settlement in principle and in an update to Part 5, Statement of Rates under Docket No. RP23-917-005, the FERC Chief Administrative Law Judge approved placing the rates from the settlement in principle in effect February 1, 2024, on an interim basis. Viking&#8217;s settlement agreement was filed with the FERC in April 2024 and (The Settlement) and was approved by the FERC on July 31, 2024. The amortization period for the deferred rate case expenses began upon FERC approval of the settlement and will be over a period of 36 months.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
